{
  "body": "TP1 embedding currently clamps IDs and converts them to int64 before lookup. This experiment folds negative-ID normalization into TileLang lookup and reads native int32/int64 strides; plain TP1 tables use TileLang too.\n\nBoth boots pass all 127 embedding checks, including 36 new public eager/graph cases. Four inspected parallel CUDA programs remain byte-identical. Of 32 public-route timing cases, three have lower means but insufficient precision on one boot; a fixed 2,048-round extension is predeclared. The patch remains draft until the zero-margin timing gates and final full-model inventories pass.\n\nRecords the exact candidate-38 base, independent patch, source equivalence, fresh application, and local checks. No promoted configuration or serving changes. Built-image, real-weight, and physical-network qualification remain separate.\n",
